Licenses of the files in lean/

1. Our own files (the Lean files in C1Challenge/ and P1*/, Release.lean, lakefile.toml, scripts/, upstream/,
   CLOSURE-SHA256SUMS, README.md): Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE-2.0). The paper and the documents
   outside lean/ stay under CC BY 4.0 (see ../LICENSE).

2. Parts taken from openai/math: some of our Lean files contain definitions or proofs copied or adapted from
   openai/math (commit 3344da59991ed94f9ba711217b29c1d760badfa6, folder lean/); their comments say so. Those parts
   remain under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE-2.0). See NOTICE.

3. patches/field-uniform.patch and patches/port-over.patch change files of openai/math. They are distributed under
   the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE-2.0). See NOTICE and patches/README.md.

4. Not distributed here: OAI/ (from openai/math, Apache License 2.0) and Lemmata/ (from ZIB-IOL/lemmata; its
   repository states no license). scripts/get-upstream.sh fetches them from their own repositories.

lean-toolchain and lake-manifest.json are build settings (the toolchain and Mathlib commits); Mathlib is under the
Apache License 2.0.
